WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.945
Normalization helps reduce repeated facts and the

00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:07.242
anomalies they can create An update anomaly

00:00:07.268 --> 00:00:09.097
occurs when the same fact appears in

00:00:09.124 --> 00:00:11.624
many rows and the copies become inconsistent

00:00:13.335 --> 00:00:15.650
An insertion anomaly occurs when you cannot

00:00:15.677 --> 00:00:18.466
store one fact without inventing another unrelated

00:00:18.493 --> 00:00:22.944
fact A deletion anomaly occurs when removing

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:25.654
one record accidentally removes the only copy

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.810
of some other important information The general

00:00:29.823 --> 00:00:31.336
goal is to store each fact in

00:00:31.362 --> 00:00:33.257
a place that matches what determines that

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:37.984
fact Normalization is not about splitting tables

00:00:38.011 --> 00:00:41.066
into as many pieces as possible It

00:00:41.092 --> 00:00:43.671
is about making dependencies clearer so updates

00:00:43.816 --> 00:00:46.579
inserts and deletes do not accidentally damage

00:00:46.606 --> 00:00:47.961
unrelated information
